<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity rpg">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">RPG Build</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~20 min</span>
    </div>

    <h3>Part 4: Make It Real — Generate a Full Party</h3>

    <p>
        One character is fine. A party of four is a game. Create a
        <code>CharacterTester.java</code> with a main method that generates
        and displays a full adventuring party.
    </p>

    <p><strong>Requirements:</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li>Create 4 Character objects</li>
        <li>Name them (Grog the Warrior, Elara the Mage, etc.)</li>
        <li>Call <code>generateStats()</code> on each</li>
        <li>Call <code>printCharacterSheet()</code> on each</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="tinker">
        <h3>Tinker: The Weakest Link</h3>
        <p>
            After generating all four characters, find and print the name of
            the character with the LOWEST total HP and the character with the
            HIGHEST strength. You'll need to compare values across objects.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Final Socratic Checkpoint — Unit 2 Kickoff</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Trace through the entire Character Creator. Where is the
                three-step pattern? Which section of the pattern is in
                <code>Character.java</code> vs <code>CharacterTester.java</code>?</li>
            <li>You use <code>Dice.statRoll()</code> in your Character class.
                How is this different from copying the Math.random() formula
                directly into Character.java?</li>
            <li>If you wanted to add an Elf race that gets +2 DEX and -1 CON,
                where would you add that logic?</li>
            <li>You've now started Unit 2. What patterns, habits, and mental
                models do you want to carry through the rest of Unit 2?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="checklist">
        <h3>Checkpoint — before moving on, you must be able to:</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Create and configure multiple instances of a class</li>
            <li>Call methods on objects from a separate tester class</li>
            <li>Compare values across objects (highest/lowest)</li>
            <li>Explain the full architecture: Dice.java → Character.java → CharacterTester.java</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

